Patch 7914 (experimental, rollback netcode): a gate sequence that the rollback snapshot can wait on instead of polling
(installer/port/jsp/jsp_snapshot_sync.h, gate_ev). Disarmed by default; the netcode keeps the polling wait unless JSP_SNAPSHOT_GATE=ev.

Change: sys_snapshot_census.c: struct ps3_gate_line_t g_ps3_gate_line (one 64-byte line holding everything the sites write: the sequence,
the waiter count and 12 per-site counters; g_ps3_gate_armed sits on another line), ps3_gate_bump(site) (seq_cst increment, WakeByAddressAll
only while the port waits), ps3_gate_arm(on, park lrs, n), ps3_gate_arm_transit(nids, n), ps3_gate_bump_counts(out[12]); site 0 in
ps3_hle_mark_enter when the lr is a parked role's lr; site 7 in ps3_hle_mark_leave after the depth drop when the frame left is a transit.
cellGcmSys.c: site 1 where cellGcm_request_tick / cellGcmTickFlip set the flip pending bit, site 2 where the flip pump marks the flip
DONE, site 3 where the FIFO drain publishes a new get equal to put. spu_workload.c: site 4 when job-chain jobs in flight drop to 0.
cellFiber.c: site 5 when a fiber enters cellFiberPpuWaitSignal. ppu_sysprx.cpp: site 6 in lwm_release; and the lwmutex census caches the
readability of each guest page (one VirtualQuery per page instead of per lwmutex), dropped by ps3_lwm_census_invalidate().
Sites not covered (a wait for them ends by the port's timeout): sys_mutex / sys_rwlock release, SPURS job-queue pending, the fiber
scheduler lock, the flip lock and the pending bits other than the flip bit.
Disarmed (the default), every site is one relaxed load.

